---
// src/pages/_site-updates/2026-10-04-founders-partnership-ack-v2.astro
export const updateMeta = {
  date: '2026-10-04',
  title: 'Founders partnership acknowledgment asks for the commitment only after the tour',
  tags: ['waitlist', 'lead-capture', 'founders'],
};
---
<article class="border-l-4 border-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] pl-6">
  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1">October 4, 2026</h2>
  <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-4">
    The required partnership acknowledgment on the Founders application at
    <a href="/pricing" class="text-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] hover:underline">/pricing</a> now reads:
    "I understand the Founders' Program is a working partnership. If we both decide it's a good
    fit after the tour, I'll be asked to run my program on BreederHQ, join the working sessions
    and share honest feedback."
  </p>

  <div class="mb-4">
    <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-1">Why</h3>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">
      The earlier wording asked an applicant to commit to the program before they had seen the
      tour. The new wording acknowledges what the partnership is and says the commitment is asked
      for only once both sides decide it is a fit.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div>
    <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-1">How it works</h3>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">
      The checkbox stays required and validates as before. The page now sends the version of the
      wording it rendered, <code>founders-partnership-v2</code>, and <code>/api/contact</code>
      records it only if it is a version the site shipped. A page opened before this change sends
      no version and is recorded as <code>founders-partnership-v1</code>, the wording it showed;
      any other value is refused with a request to refresh the page.
    </p>
  </div>
</article>
